{
  "abstract": "Formalizes the subgroup-separability (LERF) consequence of Marshall Hall's theorem for finitely generated subgroups of finitely generated free groups. The proof extracts the finitely many suffix states of a subgroup generating set and a separating word, completes the resulting partial generator actions to permutations of a finite state set, and takes the stabilizer of the base state. This is the finite-state form of the Stallings core-completion argument.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Arthur Freitas Ramos"
    }
  ],
